From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:12:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: ti,tas27xx: Add SDZ-supply and an SDZ
 fault group

The tas2764 driver already takes an optional SDZ supply, which the
binding does not describe. Apple machines drive the SDZ pins of all
their amplifiers from one line: the J616s (MacBook Pro 16" M4 Pro) has
six SN012776 on a single shutdown GPIO, modelled as a fixed regulator
that every amp takes as its SDZ-supply.

Document SDZ-supply, and apple,sdz-group-fail-closed: the amplifiers
that share an SDZ supply and carry the property form a group, and an
over-temperature or over-current fault on any of them turns the shared
supply off for the whole group. A member must have the supply and must
not have a shutdown GPIO of its own, which would bypass it.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
index fcaae848e7..f48d3f3750 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@ description: |
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: dai-common.yaml#
+  - if:
+      required:
+        - apple,sdz-group-fail-closed
+    then:
+      properties:
+        shutdown-gpios: false
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -42,6 +48,20 @@ properties:
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  SDZ-supply:
+    description:
+      Regulator that drives the SDZ (shutdown) pin, an alternative to
+      shutdown-gpios for a line that several amplifiers share.
+
+  apple,sdz-group-fail-closed:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The amplifier belongs to the group of amplifiers that share its
+      SDZ-supply. An over-temperature or over-current fault on any member
+      turns the shared supply off, which shuts every amplifier of the group
+      down, and no member enables it again until the driver is reloaded.
+      A member needs its fault interrupt.
+
   ti,imon-slot-no:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description: TDM TX current sense time slot.
@@ -59,6 +79,10 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - reg
 
+dependencies:
+  apple,sdz-group-fail-closed:
+    - SDZ-supply
+
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
